gin":"normanmaurer","id":439362,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzOTM2Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/439362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer","html_url":"https://github.com/normanmaurer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":0,"closed_issues":90,"state":"closed","created_at":"2013-03-23T06:40:07Z","updated_at":"2013-09-05T14:53:06Z","due_on":"2013-05-08T07:00:00Z","closed_at":"2013-05-08T15:33:12Z"},"comments":3,"created_at":"2013-03-23T00:55:48Z","updated_at":"2013-03-23T10:26:34Z","closed_at":"2013-03-23T10:26:18Z","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"ByteBuf.wrappedBuffer(ByteBuffer buffer) assumes that if a buffer does not have an array it is direct.  But, read-only ByteBuffers block array access.\n\nAs a contrived example, this fails:\nByteBuf.wrappedBuffer(ByteBuffer.allocate(16).asReadOnlyBuffer());\n\nIncidentally, the reason I'm finding these bugs is (I think) because I'm not working with ByteBuf other than in classes that are part of the Netty pipeline.  In Netty 3, I would have used ByteBuf everywhere, but with Netty 4 I have to be careful because if I pass one of my \"application\" ByteBufs to an encoder, then I have to duplicate().retain() it first, or the encoder will free it after writing.  Similarly I have to be careful not to retain any ByteBuf sources from any decoder, because it will also be freed if I forget to call retain().  I find it easiest to enforce this by copying in and out of nio ByteBuffers.  Am I missing a trick here?\n\nThanks for fixing all these bugs :-)\n","closed_by":{"login":"normanmaurer","id":439362,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQzOTM2Mg==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/439362?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer","html_url":"https://github.com/normanmaurer","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/normanmaurer/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/1195/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/netty/netty/issues/1195/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"completed"}